# 2026-08-13 Webhook response error

## What I was trying to do
I was trying to setup a webhook node in n8n

## What broke
When I tried entering test data to see if the webhook worked, it threw an error back at me

## What I thought was wrong
I thought the setting was somehow wrong.

## What was actually wrong
I had to switch the respond settings, once I put it to 'immediately' it started working.

## How I found it
I got to the error when I tried to submit my own form on a localhost, and I looked up what was wrong. 
## Takeaway
My takeaway with this one is that a "respond to webhook" setting has to actually match what's built in the workflow, directing it at a node that isn't there yet makes it stay, even if the setting is the right thing to choose later on. 
